{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useIsRestoring(): Box<boolean>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts#L23","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts:23"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PersistQueryClientProvider"},{"type":"text","value":", you can also use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useIsRestoring"},{"type":"text","value":" function alongside it to\ncheck if a restore is currently in progress. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and friends also check this internally to avoid\nrace conditions between the restore and mounting queries."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Box"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A reactive box — read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".current"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while a persisted client is being restored, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"\notherwise."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { useIsRestoring } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const isRestoring = useIsRestoring()\n</script>\n\n{#if isRestoring.current}\n  <div>Restoring cached data...</div>\n{/if}","lang":"svelte"}],"headings":[{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useIsRestoring(): Box<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts:23](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts#L23)\n\nIf you are using `PersistQueryClientProvider`, you can also use the `useIsRestoring` function alongside it to\ncheck if a restore is currently in progress. `createQuery` and friends also check this internally to avoid\nrace conditions between the restore and mounting queries.\n\n## Returns\n\n`Box`\\<`boolean`\\>\n\nA reactive box — read `.current` for `true` while a persisted client is being restored, `false`\notherwise.\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { useIsRestoring } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const isRestoring = useIsRestoring()\n</script>\n\n{#if isRestoring.current}\n  <div>Restoring cached data...</div>\n{/if}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useIsRestoring\ntitle: useIsRestoring\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useIsRestoring(): Box<boolean>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts:23](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/svelte-query/src/useIsRestoring.ts#L23)\n\nIf you are using `PersistQueryClientProvider`, you can also use the `useIsRestoring` function alongside it to\ncheck if a restore is currently in progress. `createQuery` and friends also check this internally to avoid\nrace conditions between the restore and mounting queries.\n\n## Returns\n\n`Box`\\<`boolean`\\>\n\nA reactive box — read `.current` for `true` while a persisted client is being restored, `false`\notherwise.\n\n## Example\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { useIsRestoring } from '@tanstack/svelte-query'\n\n  const isRestoring = useIsRestoring()\n</script>\n\n{#if isRestoring.current}\n  <div>Restoring cached data...</div>\n{/if}\n```\n"}
